IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa12-logic`

-- coa12-ch5-concerns.l4: the Companies Act 2006, Part 16, Chapter 5 "Quoted companies: right of members to raise audit concerns at
-- accounts meeting": ss 527, 528, 529, 530, 531 (lines 7416-7463 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- See coa12-ch3a-report.l4 for how to read an answer. Forks are in NOTES.md.
-- "Working days" (s 528(4)(a)) are the keel's s 1173(1): the number of working days is an input, and the deontic rule's clock counts working days.
-- Keel and other-part answers are INPUTS named as PLAN.md 4.1 and 4.2 name them.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 531  Meaning of "quoted company" (placed first: the rest of the Chapter asks for its answer)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 531(1)
-- Plain gloss: for this Chapter a company is quoted if it is a quoted company under s 385 for the financial year the accounts to be laid at the next accounts meeting relate to.
-- src:7462 | (1) For the purposes of this Chapter a company is a quoted company if it is a quoted company in accordance with section 385 (quoted and unquoted companies for the purposes of Part 15) in relation to the financial year to which the accounts to be laid at the next accounts meeting relate.
@ref s 531(1) Quoted company for this Chapter (src:7462-7462)
GIVEN `s 385 the company is a quoted company in relation to the financial year to which the accounts to be laid at the next accounts meeting relate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 531(1) the company is a quoted company for the purposes of this Chapter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 385 the company is a quoted company in relation to the financial year to which the accounts to be laid at the next accounts meeting relate`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "For the purposes of this Chapter a company is a quoted company if it is a quoted company in accordance with section 385" (a definition by "is ... if", read as closed: marginal reading (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is quoted under s 385 (coa8) is not known

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 527  Members' power to require website publication of audit concerns
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 527(1), s 527(1)(a), s 527(1)(b), s 527(1)#L7421
-- Plain gloss: the members of a quoted company may require it to publish on a website a statement of any matter about the audit of the accounts to be laid before the next accounts meeting, or about an auditor ceasing to hold office since the previous accounts meeting, that they propose to raise at the next accounts meeting.
-- src:7418 | (1) The members of a quoted company may require the company to publish on a website a statement setting out any matter relating to—
-- src:7419 | (a) the audit of the company's accounts (including the auditor's report and the conduct of the audit) that are to be laid before the next accounts meeting, or
-- src:7420 | (b) any circumstances connected with an auditor of the company ceasing to hold office since the previous accounts meeting,
-- src:7421 | that the members propose to raise at the next accounts meeting of the company.
@ref s 527(1) The members' power to require website publication (src:7418-7421)
GIVEN `s 531(1) the company is a quoted company for the purposes of this Chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement sets out a matter relating to the audit of the company's accounts (including the auditor's report and the conduct of the audit) that are to be laid before the next accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement sets out a matter relating to any circumstances connected with an auditor of the company ceasing to hold office since the previous accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the members propose to raise the matter at the next accounts meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 527(1) the members may require the company to publish the statement on a website` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 531(1) the company is a quoted company for the purposes of this Chapter`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF (`the statement sets out a matter relating to the audit of the company's accounts (including the auditor's report and the conduct of the audit) that are to be laid before the next accounts meeting` OR `the statement sets out a matter relating to any circumstances connected with an auditor of the company ceasing to hold office since the previous accounts meeting`) AND `the members propose to raise the matter at the next accounts meeting of the company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any matter relating to— (a) the audit of the company's accounts ... or (b) any circumstances connected with an auditor of the company ceasing to hold office ..., that the members propose to raise at the next accounts meeting"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The members of a quoted company may require"; the power is given to the members of a quoted company and the subsection says nothing of any other company
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company rests on s 385 (coa8), not known

-- COVERS-FORK F15: s 527(2), s 527(2)(a), s 527(2)(b)
-- Plain gloss: the company is required to publish once it has received requests from members holding at least 5% of the voting rights of all members who can vote at the accounts meeting (treasury shares left out), or from at least 100 such members holding shares with an average of at least 100 pounds paid up per member.
-- src:7422 | (2) A company is required to do so once it has received requests to that effect from—
-- src:7423 | (a) members representing at least 5% of the total voting rights of all the members who have a relevant right to vote (excluding any voting rights attached to any shares in the company held as treasury shares), or
-- src:7424 | (b) at least 100 members who have a relevant right to vote and hold shares in the company on which there has been paid up an average sum, per member, of at least £100.
@ref s 527(2) When the company is required to publish (src:7422-7424)
GIVEN `the voting rights of the requesting members, as a fraction of the total voting rights of all the members who have a relevant right to vote (excluding any voting rights attached to any shares held as treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of the requesting members who have a relevant right to vote and hold shares in the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the average sum paid up on those members' shares, per member, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 527(2) the company is required to publish the statement on a website` MEANS
    IF       `the voting rights of the requesting members, as a fraction of the total voting rights of all the members who have a relevant right to vote (excluding any voting rights attached to any shares held as treasury shares)` AT LEAST 0.05
          OR (`the number of the requesting members who have a relevant right to vote and hold shares in the company` AT LEAST 100 AND `the average sum paid up on those members' shares, per member, in pounds` AT LEAST 100)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is required to do so once it has received requests to that effect from— (a) members representing at least 5% of the total voting rights ..., or (b) at least 100 members who have a relevant right to vote and hold shares in the company on which there has been paid up an average sum, per member, of at least £100" ("once" counts as "where": the 2026-11-05 rulings; the requests counted are taken to be valid requests under subsection (4): fork F15)

-- COVERS-INERT 1: s 527(2)#L7425 | signpost: "See also section 153 (exercise of rights where shares held on behalf of others)"
-- (the closing words "See also section 153" are a signpost to s 153, which is Part 10 of another part's range; no rule of its own)

-- COVERS: s 527(3)
-- Plain gloss: a "relevant right to vote" is a right to vote at the accounts meeting.
-- src:7426 | (3) In subsection (2) a “relevant right to vote” means a right to vote at the accounts meeting.
@ref s 527(3) "relevant right to vote" (src:7426-7426)
GIVEN `the right is a right to vote at the accounts meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 527(3) the right is a relevant right to vote` MEANS
    IF `the right is a right to vote at the accounts meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “relevant right to vote” means a right to vote at the accounts meeting"

-- COVERS: s 527(4), s 527(4)(a), s 527(4)(b), s 527(4)(c), s 527(4)(d)
-- Plain gloss: a request may go by post or electronically; it must say which statement it is about, be authenticated by those making it, and reach the company at least a week before the meeting.
-- src:7427 | (4) A request—
-- src:7428 | (a) may be sent to the company in hard copy or electronic form,
-- src:7429 | (b) must identify the statement to which it relates,
-- src:7430 | (c) must be authenticated by the person or persons making it, and
-- src:7431 | (d) must be received by the company at least one week before the meeting to which it relates.
@ref s 527(4) The request (src:7427-7431)
GIVEN `how the request is sent to the company` IS A `Form of document`
      `the request identifies the statement to which it relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1146 Requirement of authentication` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date the company receives the request` IS A DATE
      `the date of the meeting to which the request relates` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 527(4) the request is a valid request` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the request identifies the statement to which it relates`) OR `the date the company receives the request` GREATER THAN (`the date of the meeting to which the request relates` MINUS 7)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A request— ... (b) must identify the statement to which it relates, ... and (d) must be received by the company at least one week before the meeting to which it relates" (fork F2 for (b); a period fixed in the text's own words for (d): the 2026-11-05 ruling (a); a request in either form, (a), is not a ground for refusing it)
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1146 Requirement of authentication`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A request— ... (c) must be authenticated by the person or persons making it" (fork F2)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the request is authenticated is section 1146 (coa25), not known

-- COVERS: s 527(5)
-- Plain gloss: a quoted company need not publish if, on an application by the company or another person claiming to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the rights are being abused. JUST FALSE here means "not required".
-- src:7432 | (5) A quoted company is not required to place on a website a statement under this section if, on an application by the company or another person who claims to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by this section are being abused.
@ref s 527(5) Abuse of the rights (src:7432-7432)
GIVEN `on an application by the company or another person who claims to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by this section are being abused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 527(5) the quoted company is required to place the statement on a website` MEANS
    IF `on an application by the company or another person who claims to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by this section are being abused`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A quoted company is not required to place on a website a statement under this section if, on an application by the company or another person who claims to be aggrieved, the court is satisfied that the rights conferred by this section are being abused"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says only when the company is not required; whether it is required is subsection (2)

-- COVERS: s 527(6)
-- Plain gloss: on such an application the court may order the members who requested publication to pay the company's costs (in Scotland, expenses), whole or part, even if they are not parties.
-- src:7433 | (6) The court may order the members requesting website publication to pay the whole or part of the company's costs (in Scotland, expenses) on such an application, even if they are not parties to the application.
@ref s 527(6) Costs (src:7433-7433)
GIVEN `an application has been made under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 527(6) the court may order the members requesting website publication to pay the company's costs on the application` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made under subsection (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may order the members requesting website publication to pay the whole or part of the company's costs ... on such an application"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 528  Requirements as to website availability
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS-INERT 1: s 528(1) | lead-in: "The following provisions apply for the purposes of section 527"; each provision that follows is encoded
-- (the lead-in "The following provisions apply for the purposes of section 527" is covered by the functions that follow)

-- COVERS: s 528(2), s 528(2)(a), s 528(2)(b)
-- Plain gloss: the information goes on a website maintained by or for the company that names the company.
-- src:7436 | (2) The information must be made available on a website that—
-- src:7437 | (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and
-- src:7438 | (b) identifies the company in question.
@ref s 528(2) The website (src:7436-7438)
GIVEN `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the website identifies the company in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 528(2) the website meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` AND `the website identifies the company in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The information must be made available on a website that— (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and (b) identifies the company in question" (fork F2)

-- COVERS: s 528(3)
-- Plain gloss: access to the information, and getting a hard copy from the website, must be free and unrestricted.
-- src:7439 | (3) Access to the information on the website, and the ability to obtain a hard copy of the information from the website, must not be conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted.
@ref s 528(3) Access (src:7439-7439)
GIVEN `access to the information on the website, or the ability to obtain a hard copy of it from the website, is conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 528(3) the access to the information meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `access to the information on the website, or the ability to obtain a hard copy of it from the website, is conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Access to the information on the website, and the ability to obtain a hard copy of the information from the website, must not be conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted" (fork F2)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- COVERS: s 528(4), s 528(4)(a)
-- Plain gloss: the statement must be made available within three working days of the company being required to publish it. The number of working days (s 1173(1), the keel's answer) is an input.
-- src:7440 | (4) The statement—
-- src:7441 | (a) must be made available within three working days of the company being required to publish it on a website, and
@ref s 528(4)(a) Within three working days (src:7440-7441)
GIVEN `the number of working days after the day the company was required to publish the statement on which it was made available` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 528(4)(a) the statement was made available within three working days of the company being required to publish it` MEANS
    IF `the number of working days after the day the company was required to publish the statement on which it was made available` AT LEAST 0 AND `the number of working days after the day the company was required to publish the statement on which it was made available` AT MOST 3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be made available within three working days of the company being required to publish it on a website" (a period fixed in the text's own words: the 2026-11-05 ruling (a); the count of working days is the keel's s 1173(1))

-- The same duty as a deontic rule. The unit of its clock is the working day (s 1173(1), the keel), NOT the calendar day: day 0 is the day the
-- company is required to publish, and the trace is read with every day counted as a working day.
@ref s 528(4)(a) Within three working days (src:7441-7441)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 528(4)(a) the company's duty to make the statement available on a website` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "make the statement available on a website within three working days of being required to publish it"
    WITHIN 3
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 528(4)(a): the statement was not made available within three working days of the company being required to publish it"

-- COVERS: s 528(4)(b)
-- Plain gloss: and it must be kept available until after the meeting.
-- src:7440 | (4) The statement—
-- src:7442 | (b) must be kept available until after the meeting to which it relates.
@ref s 528(4)(b) Kept available until after the meeting (src:7440-7442)
GIVEN `the statement was kept available until after the meeting to which it relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 528(4)(b) the statement was kept available until after the meeting to which it relates` MEANS
    IF `the statement was kept available until after the meeting to which it relates`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be kept available until after the meeting to which it relates" (fork F2)

-- COVERS: s 528(5), s 528(5)(a), s 528(5)(b)
-- Plain gloss: a failure to keep the information available throughout is ignored if it was available for part of the period and the failure is wholly due to circumstances the company could not reasonably have been expected to prevent or avoid.
-- src:7443 | (5) A failure to make information available on a website throughout the period specified in subsection (4)(b) is disregarded if—
-- src:7444 | (a) the information is made available on the website for part of that period, and
-- src:7445 | (b) the failure is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid.
@ref s 528(5) A failure that is disregarded (src:7443-7445)
GIVEN `the information is made available on the website for part of the period specified in subsection (4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 528(5) the failure to make the information available throughout the period is disregarded` MEANS
    IF `the information is made available on the website for part of the period specified in subsection (4)(b)` AND `the failure is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A failure to make information available on a website throughout the period specified in subsection (4)(b) is disregarded if— (a) ..., and (b) ..." (marginal reading (a))

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 529  Website publication: company's supplementary duties
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 529(1), s 529(1)(a), s 529(1)(b)
-- Plain gloss: a quoted company must, in the notice of the accounts meeting, draw attention to the possibility of a statement being placed on a website at members' request and to the effect of the rest of s 529.
-- src:7447 | (1) A quoted company must in the notice it gives of the accounts meeting draw attention to—
-- src:7448 | (a) the possibility of a statement being placed on a website in pursuance of members' requests under section 527, and
-- src:7449 | (b) the effect of the following provisions of this section.
@ref s 529(1) The notice of the accounts meeting (src:7447-7449)
GIVEN `s 531(1) the company is a quoted company for the purposes of this Chapter` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 529(1) the quoted company must draw attention in the notice of the accounts meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 531(1) the company is a quoted company for the purposes of this Chapter`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A quoted company must in the notice it gives of the accounts meeting draw attention to"; the subsection says nothing of any other company
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company rests on s 385 (coa8), not known

@ref s 529(1)(a)-(b) What the notice must draw attention to (src:7448-7449)
GIVEN `the notice draws attention to the possibility of a statement being placed on a website in pursuance of members' requests under section 527` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice draws attention to the effect of the following provisions of section 529` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 529(1) the notice draws attention to what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice draws attention to the possibility of a statement being placed on a website in pursuance of members' requests under section 527` AND `the notice draws attention to the effect of the following provisions of section 529`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must in the notice it gives of the accounts meeting draw attention to— (a) the possibility of a statement being placed on a website ..., and (b) the effect of the following provisions of this section" (fork F2)

-- COVERS: s 529(2)
-- Plain gloss: the company may not make the requesting members pay its expenses of complying with s 527 or 528.
-- src:7450 | (2) A company may not require the members requesting website publication to pay its expenses in complying with that section or section 528 (requirements in connection with website publication).
@ref s 529(2) No expenses (src:7450-7450)
GIVEN `the expenses are the company's expenses in complying with section 527 or section 528` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 529(2) the company may require the members requesting website publication to pay its expenses` MEANS
    IF `the expenses are the company's expenses in complying with section 527 or section 528`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company may not require the members requesting website publication to pay its expenses in complying with that section or section 528"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of those expenses

-- Time of day, as a record: the day and the hour (0 to 24) at which something is done. The stable binary's DATETIME needs imports that fail on both builds.
DECLARE `s 529(3) time` HAS
    `the day` IS A DATE
    `the hour of the day` IS A NUMBER

-- COVERS: s 529(3)
-- Plain gloss: where the company is required to put a statement on a website it must send it to the company's auditor no later than the moment it makes it available.
-- src:7451 | (3) Where a company is required to place a statement on a website under section 527 it must forward the statement to the company's auditor not later than the time when it makes the statement available on the website.
@ref s 529(3) The statement goes to the auditor (src:7451-7451)
GIVEN `the company is required to place a statement on a website under section 527` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 529(3) the company must forward the statement to the company's auditor` MEANS
    IF `the company is required to place a statement on a website under section 527`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company is required to place a statement on a website under section 527 it must forward the statement to the company's auditor" (the 2026-11-05 ruling on "where")

@ref s 529(3) Not later than the time the statement is made available (src:7451-7451)
GIVEN `the time the statement was forwarded to the auditor` IS A MAYBE `s 529(3) time`
      `the time the statement was made available on the website` IS A `s 529(3) time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 529(3) the statement was forwarded to the auditor not later than the time it was made available on the website` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the time the statement was forwarded to the auditor`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must forward the statement to the company's auditor not later than the time when it makes the statement available on the website" (it was not forwarded)
    WHEN JUST t THEN
        IF (t's `the day`) LESS THAN (`the time the statement was made available on the website`'s `the day`)
           OR ((t's `the day`) EQUALS (`the time the statement was made available on the website`'s `the day`) AND (t's `the hour of the day`) AT MOST (`the time the statement was made available on the website`'s `the hour of the day`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than the time when it makes the statement available on the website"

-- The same duty as a deontic rule. "Not later than the time when it makes the statement available" is a time relative to another act, not a
-- number of days, so there is no WITHIN.
@ref s 529(3) The statement goes to the auditor (src:7451-7451)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 529(3) the company's duty to forward the statement to the auditor` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` OF Company, Auditor, "forward the statement to the company's auditor"
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- COVERS: s 529(4)
-- Plain gloss: the business that may be dealt with at the accounts meeting includes any statement the company has been required under s 527 to publish.
-- src:7452 | (4) The business which may be dealt with at the accounts meeting includes any statement that the company has been required under section 527 to publish on a website.
@ref s 529(4) Business at the accounts meeting (src:7452-7452)
GIVEN `the statement is one that the company has been required under section 527 to publish on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 529(4) the business which may be dealt with at the accounts meeting includes the statement` MEANS
    IF `the statement is one that the company has been required under section 527 to publish on a website`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The business which may be dealt with at the accounts meeting includes any statement that the company has been required under section 527 to publish on a website"; other business is not decided here

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 530  Website publication: offences
-- =========================================================================================================

-- COVERS: s 530(1), s 530(1)(a), s 530(1)(b), s 530(1)#L7457
-- Plain gloss: in the event of default in complying with s 528 or s 529, every officer of the company who is in default commits an offence.
-- src:7454 | (1) In the event of default in complying with
-- src:7455 | (a) section 528 (requirements as to website publication), or
-- src:7456 | (b) section 529 (companies' supplementary duties in relation to request for website publication),
-- src:7457 | an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 530(1) The offence (src:7454-7457)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 528 (requirements as to website publication)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `default is made in complying with section 529 (companies' supplementary duties in relation to request for website publication)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 530(1) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 528 (requirements as to website publication)` OR `default is made in complying with section 529 (companies' supplementary duties in relation to request for website publication)`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default` -- JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE (not in default: section 1121), or NOTHING where section 1121 is not known
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the event of default in complying with (a) section 528 ..., or (b) section 529 ... an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default" (marginal reading (a))

-- COVERS: s 530(2), s 530(2)(a), s 530(2)(b)
-- Plain gloss: the penalty: on indictment a fine; on summary conviction a fine up to the statutory maximum.
-- src:7458 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:7459 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:7460 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 530(2) The penalty (src:7458-7460)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 530(2) the penalty for an offence under this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF mode, NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE JUST (Penalty OF mode, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
